# Files Fern must not modify or delete when regenerating this repo.
#
# Fern prunes anything it did not generate, and it reads this file from the pull request's
# base branch — so an entry only protects a file once it is on main.
#
# publish-main.yml is hand-written: it releases whop_sdk when a merge to main lands a
# lib/whop_sdk/version.rb that is not yet on RubyGems. It is the only publish path, and it
# authenticates with the GEM_HOST_API_KEY secret.
#
# ci.yml is hand-written for a security reason, not a stylistic one. The Fern Ruby
# generator emits a ci.yml containing an unconditional `publish` job: it fires on any
# refs/tags/* push — including the tag publish-main.yml creates — runs `bundle install`
# in a job holding `id-token: write`, and ends in `gem push`. That is a second, unreviewed
# publish path and a credential-minting hazard in the same job as third-party install
# scripts. Ruby is the only Fern language that does this; the generated ci.yml in
# whopsdk-typescript and whopsdk-python is compile+test only. Ours is the generated file
# with the publish job removed.
#
# CHANGELOG.md predates the cutover and holds 41 Stainless releases. Fern does not write
# one, so without this entry that history would disappear from the tree on the first
# generated PR.
.github/workflows/ci.yml
.github/workflows/publish-main.yml
CHANGELOG.md
